      "message": "Concern - required before merge: this call sits outside the try/except above. QuadsBase.get raises APIBadRequest on a 400 (quads_api.py:55-64), and the new route returns 400 when the assignment has no notification row; in cli/main.py only CliException is handled cleanly (main.py:68 -\u003e exit 2), anything else reaches logger.exception at main.py:80 -\u003e full traceback, exit 1. Agree with Ted and Will here.\n\nCheaper alternative: get_active_cloud_assignment already embeds the notification (Assignment.as_dict serializes it, models.py:108-111; create_assignment always attaches one, dao/assignment.py:31; 7 existing callsites use assignment.notification.id), so `notification_id \u003d assignment.notification.id` with a CliException guard for a missing notification removes the new endpoint and the second HTTP call entirely - and the 400 exposure with them. If the endpoint stays, wrap the call in the existing try/except and keep a None guard.\n\nEither way, please add a divergent-id regression test: tests/cli/test_notifications.py passes on parent too, because a fresh DB keeps assignment.id \u003d\u003d notification.id in lockstep, so the suite cannot catch a regression of this bug today. (Fix behavior verified live by Will: old code PATCHed the orphan notification; the new flow resolves the correct one.)",
      "revId": "d59746b79c27d26357ecae3aab825bd6c826360d",
